// A road with a dip and a fenced ember, the seed in an ember's pit, the stone on a pillar, a ladder beside a rising ember; four generations of bloom become a mesa to a high road with the door at its end.
name Origin
rule B1234/S012345678
steps 4
hint The seed lies in the pit where an ember paces. The stone stands on the pillar; the ladder beside it climbs past a rising ember, and a boulder bridges to the top. Plant, come back down the ladder, Grow, then climb the bloom to the high road.
tip Four generations reach four cells out from the stone in every direction. Wait on the ladder below the bloom's reach, at least five cells under the stone, before you grow. One last ember walks the high road.
intro The highest stone in the deepest cave. You have found where every ruin began. This is where you began: a seed in a pit, a stone on a pillar, and an ember rising and falling between them.
outro The last bloom grew from the highest point, and you climbed it into the light. You were its seed.
